**Factual Observations:**  
- MAIT cells are characterized by their semi-invariant TCRs, primarily composed of Vα7.2-Jα33 in humans [MDC759BC86720 p1].  
- MAIT cells recognize riboflavin metabolites produced by bacteria and fungi, presented by the MR1 molecule [MDC759BC86720 p2].  
- In HCC, MAIT cells display an exhausted phenotype with reduced IFN-γ production [MDC759BC86720 p5].  
- The use of MAIT cells in cancer immunotherapy is highlighted, including their potential to be generated from iPSCs [MDC759BC86720 p8].